{
  "dom_id": "step-q76000",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-2>6 \\\\ 2x-9\\le 5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $4x-2>6$ and $2x-9\\le 5$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $4x-2>6\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & >6 \\\\ 4x-2+2 & >6+2 \\\\ 4x & >8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & >\\frac{8}{4} \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/59523e51144ef776295ec43032def1bc0192351deb6294fbb2d56acd87bb2cac.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2x-9\\le 5\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-9 & \\le 5 \\\\ 2x-9+9 & \\le 5 \\\\ 2x & \\le 14 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{14}{2} \\\\ x & \\le 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/b0107bec7ccb2c56036de405a29870e8cfcc166cc6405f425fc3296ec8f1be2b.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/f9ace3f6dd9d93b960c61bb31ca3858aefbb0e8d43f2392a643c078ae6111a0d.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $2<x\\le 7.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
